<title>USA: Valve snag keeps CMS 67 MW Mich. unit shut.</title>
<headline>Valve snag keeps CMS 67 MW Mich. unit shut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co's 67 megawatt (MW) Big Rock Point 1 nuclear plant in Charlevoix, Mich., remained shut after its admission valves unexpectedly shut Monday, the Nulear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The generating station was taken out off line Sept 10 for approximately six days to repair a valve leak.</p>
<p>No estimated restart date for Big Rock Point 1 was given and the company was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Consumers is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
